      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Algerian struggle for independence was long and intense, beginning with escalating nationalist fervor in the 1930s. A major turning point was the rise of the FLN in the 1950s, which initiated armed resistance against French rule. The outbreak of the full-scale war in 1954 marked a profound commitment to armed liberation from the colonial system. Key moments, like the Battle of Algiers, demonstrated the fierce determination of the resistance against French military dominance. Ultimately, international pressure and sustained popular uprising forced France to grant Algerian sovereignty in 1962.",
