      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Prior to 1954, deep socioeconomic injustices fueled the growing discontent with French colonial rule. Native Algerians faced systematic discrimination, being relegated to second-class citizenship despite being inhabitants of the land. Land ownership was heavily skewed toward European settlers, leading to poverty and dispossession among the indigenous population. Political avenues for true representation were systematically blocked, convincing many that only radical, armed struggle could dismantle the oppressive colonial structure. This confluence of political disenfranchisement and economic exploitation made revolution the undeniable necessity for self-determination.",
      "source": "target",
